Logging system ideas:

- Data points:
	+ Time
	+ Path, Class, Method
	+ Level
	+ Name

- Grouping logs,
	+ create a group
	+ submit log entry to group (maybe output? maybe just locally?)
	+ finalize group
	+ output and store as group of logs

- Indent logs,
	+ When using sub-processes (methods) use indentation for a better visualization of the process.

- Root group,
	+ When using the grouping system, setup a group as a root.
		This will be an origin point for the indentation and the group with which, once finalized, it will be outputted and stored.

- Sub groups == indents

--------------------------------------------------

Startup,
	- Open root group
	- Send opening log entry
	- Set configs through method

Input,
	- Async usability
	- Log entry
		- Header data
			- Time
			- Path, Class, Method
			- Severity level
			- Group
			- Name
		- Content data
			- Provided information
	- Opening a group
	- Closing a group

Process,
	- Queue for synchronization, throw error if queue gets too big
	- Format log entry

Output,
	- Console
		- Toggle information
			- if "Time" is shown, What information of the given time (date, time, etc.)
			- if "Path, Class, Method" is shown
			- What "Severity level" and above it should show
			- if "Group" is shown, if it shows just the "Group" or also the "Group path"
			- if "Name" is shown'
		- Output on trigger
	- File
		- Doesn't take file into cache, Write only: FileOutputStream
	- Custom
		- Raw logs get sent to registered custom output sources. (usage example, network logging)

Shutdown,
	- Finish processes & output
	- Prevent new inputs
	- Output in batches

--------------------------------------------------

